---
import Base from "@layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHero from "@components/PageHero.astro";
import Section from "@components/Section.astro";
import Card from "@components/Card.astro";
import CTA from "@components/CTA.astro";
import { SITE } from "@data/site";

const artifacts = [
  {
    path: "config/mainnet/",
    note: "Final canonical allocations and the genesis publication bundle for mainnet launch.",
  },
  {
    path: "_docs/operations/mainnet-go-no-go-decision.md",
    note: "The formal launch decision record — status, rationale, and scheduled windows.",
  },
  {
    path: "RELEASE.md · VERIFICATION.md",
    note: "Release engineering and artifact verification posture for tagged releases.",
  },
  {
    path: "docs/COMPATIBILITY.md",
    note: "Version and deployment compatibility guidance for operators.",
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Network — VirtEngine"
  description="VirtEngine network status: TestNet is planned for January 2027 and MainNet for March 2027, with separate validation and production approval gates."
  path="/network"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: "Home", href: "/" },
    { name: "Network", href: "/network" },
  ]}
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Network status"
    title="A two-stage path to production"
    lede="This page reports exactly what the repository records — no more, no less. The repository is the source of truth for network status."
    crumbs={[
      { name: "Home", href: "/" },
      { name: "Network", href: "/network" },
    ]}
  />

  <Section eyebrow="Launch posture" title="TestNet in January; MainNet in March">
    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      <div class="reveal rounded-card border border-green-soft bg-green-wash p-6">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-slate">Current status</p>
        <p class="mt-2 font-display text-3xl text-green-deep">Preparing</p>
        <p class="mt-1.5 font-mono text-xs text-muted">not live</p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal rounded-card border border-line bg-panel p-6">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-slate">TestNet</p>
        <p class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl text-ink">January 2027</p>
        <p class="mt-1.5 font-mono text-xs text-muted">public pre-production</p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal rounded-card border border-line bg-panel p-6">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-slate">MainNet</p>
        <p class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl text-ink">March 2027</p>
        <p class="mt-1.5 font-mono text-xs text-muted">production, after approval</p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal rounded-card border border-line bg-panel p-6">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-slate">Genesis bundle</p>
        <p class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl text-ink">Checked in</p>
        <p class="mt-1.5 font-mono text-xs text-muted">config/mainnet/</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-body reveal mt-8 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-base">
      <p>
        <strong>TestNet is planned for January 2027.</strong> It is a public proving
        environment for validators, providers, integrations, upgrades, recovery, VEID,
        marketplace, and settlement flows. Its state may be reset, its tokens have no
        production value, and its data is not guaranteed to carry into MainNet.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>MainNet is planned for March 2027.</strong> It is the persistent
        production network and requires successful TestNet exit evidence, final
        artifacts, and a fresh go/no-go approval. Exact UTC dates will be confirmed
        through the formal launch process; neither network is live until officially
        announced.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Why two stages" title="Validate, remediate, then promote">
    <div class="prose-body reveal max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-base">
      <p>
        The separation is an explicit safety gate. January produces real
        multi-operator TestNet evidence. February is reserved for observation,
        fixing and re-testing defects, completing security and operational reviews,
        freezing the production release, and coordinating the final validator set.
      </p>
      <p>
        March is the MainNet window only after those exit criteria are met. A
        successful TestNet launch does not automatically approve MainNet; release
        management must record a separate production decision.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section
    eyebrow="Artifacts"
    title="Where the launch materials live"
    lede="Everything an operator needs to verify is in the repository:"
  >
    <ul class="grid gap-3 lg:grid-cols-2">
      {
        artifacts.map((item) => (
          <li class="reveal rounded-card border border-line bg-panel px-5 py-4">
            <code class="font-mono text-sm font-medium text-green-deep">{item.path}</code>
            <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm text-slate">{item.note}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Parameters" title="Network parameters are chain state">
    <div class="prose-body reveal max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-base">
      <p>
        Economic and operational parameters — inflation band, staking targets, take
        rate, unbonding period, approved clients — are defined by the protocol's default
        parameters and governed on-chain thereafter. The defaults are documented on the
        <a href="/protocol">protocol page</a> and in
        <a href={SITE.docs}>the documentation</a>; live values on a running network
        always take precedence and are queryable from any node.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section eyebrow="Operators" title="Preparing to validate at launch">
    <div class="grid gap-5 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <Card title="Verify before you run" class="reveal p-8">
        Confirm the release tag you intend to install has actually been published, that
        the target network has an approved launch or upgrade decision, and that the
        verification posture in <code class="font-mono text-[0.85em] text-green-deep">VERIFICATION.md</code> matches
        your deployment. Genesis materials should be validated against the published
        bundle in <code class="font-mono text-[0.85em] text-green-deep">config/mainnet/</code>.
      </Card>
      <Card title="Validator onboarding" class="reveal p-8">
        The validator role, economics, dual consensus-plus-identity duties, and slashing
        model are covered on the staking page, with operational guides in the
        documentation. Start there, then coordinate with the validator community through
        the repository.
      </Card>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
      <CTA href="/staking">Validator &amp; staking overview</CTA>
      <CTA href="/learn/mainnet-roadmap" variant="secondary">The road to mainnet, explained</CTA>
      <CTA href={SITE.github} variant="ghost">Decision record on GitHub</CTA>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>
